course: dictionary
lesson: 7481
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings, and position is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «A sundial tells the time from the position of a shadow.» Here position means the place where the shadow is.
explain: Position can also mean the way a body or thing is placed. «Sitting in any one position for hours does harm, so get up, stretch and move often.» Here position means the way you sit, stand or lie.
explain: Position can mean a place in a race, a role in a team, or a job. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Position is a noun and a verb: a position is a place or way of being placed, and to position something means to put it carefully in a place.
fact: «A satnav or phone finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites in orbit.»
fact: The position of the sun changes across the sky during the day.
fact: In place value, the position of a digit tells you its value: the 3 in 352 is in the hundreds position.
fact: Phrases with position include in position, out of position, the recovery position, first position, and in a difficult position.
exercise: «A sundial tells the time from the position of a shadow.» In this sentence, what does position mean? | A job in an office | The way a dog sits | *The place where the shadow is | A winning prize
exercise: «She finished in second position in the race.» What does position mean? | *The place she came in the race | The way she was lying down | The role she played in her team | A signal from a satellite
exercise: What does it mean to position something? | To throw it away | To paint it a bright colour | *To put it carefully in a place | To count it up
test: «Sitting in any one position for hours does harm, so move often.» What does position mean here? | A signal from a satellite | A place on a map | A result in a race | *The way your body is placed
test: Goalkeeper is a position in football. What does position mean? | A place where the ball can fly | A type of goal | *A role a player covers in a team | A kind of football boot
exam: Which sentence uses position to mean a job? | The sundial showed the position of the shadow | He lay in the recovery position on the floor | *She applied for the position of office manager | The position of the sun changed through the day
